WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.060
Film Courage: What are five thing a director
should never do on set?

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:08.470
Chloe Carroll, Actor/Director: No know the
story, not understand the scene completely

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:15.820
so when an actor asks the question they are
like “I don’t know?”

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:22.330
Not put an actor under pressure because of
the time constraints of production to get

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:23.630
a performance.

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:30.970
Obviously you will need to get the shot in
time but I think by not letting the actor

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:38.530
be aware of the set and the time constraints
is really helpful because you’re not…I

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:43.190
think without the pressure they will give
a better performance and to try and keep that

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:44.969
separate.

00:00:44.969 --> 00:00:48.760
I think that is why the director is really
the only person who talks to the actors.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:54.379
They are not in the conversations with the
camera person and the camera person would

00:00:54.379 --> 00:00:55.489
talk to the director.

00:00:55.489 --> 00:01:07.950
They kind of keep it all the way so they can
just concentrate on the performance.

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:13.729
I think a director has to care about the movie
so not caring about it.

00:01:13.729 --> 00:01:17.390
When you’re on the set and you can tell
that the director is not that particularly

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:23.060
or they are doing it for money and they are
not really into the story, I think it shows.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:28.700
I think a director you pick on every production
should really care about the story or be really

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:32.039
excited and want to do it.

00:01:32.039 --> 00:01:33.359
I think that is really important.

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:37.322
Film Courage: I like what you said (just real
quickly) about protecting them [the actors].

00:01:37.322 --> 00:01:44.499
So is it almost like protecting a child from
knowing certain news so then the actor is

00:01:44.499 --> 00:01:46.749
going to be protected while on set?

00:01:46.749 --> 00:01:52.399
Chloe: Yes so they don’t have to worry about
anything but the character because that was

00:01:52.399 --> 00:01:58.499
one thing with producing THE HONEYMOON PHASE
close to actually filming it.

00:01:58.499 --> 00:02:05.209
I was not doing as much producing work as
I was doing the acting so that I wasn’t

00:02:05.209 --> 00:02:11.269
like Oh my gosh now we have to do this for
tomorrow and this on set as I was acting and

00:02:11.269 --> 00:02:17.269
worrying about that too much that it’s just
like let the actor do their thing and not

00:02:17.269 --> 00:02:21.790
have their outside worries as so important
because I think that they will deliver a better

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:26.420
performance because they are not pressured
and not worried about other things.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:28.549
Their mind is only on the character.

00:02:28.549 --> 00:02:32.040
For me that’s huge.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:38.150
So if I direct…I’ve only directed little
shorts but I tried to do that.

00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:45.420
Film Courage: But I’m sure that shorts is
something that will add up.

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:49.400
Do you think you’ll ever do a feature in
the next four years.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.390
Chloe: Direct a feature?

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:52.780
I thought about it.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:53.780
Eventually.

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:55.060
I don’t know if I’ll direct.

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:56.069
I like directing.

00:02:56.069 --> 00:03:01.709
I like directing but I don’t like…it’s
so stressful I feel to direct because you

00:03:01.709 --> 00:03:10.620
are the core person on that production that
everyone looks to everything for and I think

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:16.600
if it was like a really cool horror story
I would direct but I’d have to be really

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:22.620
into it to feel like I would do it justice
as the director.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:23.799
Maybe I guess?

00:03:23.799 --> 00:03:26.849
But I prefer acting and producing they are
my two favorite things.

00:03:26.849 --> 00:03:27.379
Question: What is something a director should
never do on set?

